or the next\n  term. <kbd>Esc</kbd> takes you back.\n- <kbd>⌘ Enter</kbd> / <kbd>Ctrl Enter</kbd> opens the article’s Metadata page, and on it takes you\n  back to the article, as pressing **Metadata** again does. In a box you are typing in — a comment,\n  feedback, a quiz answer — it saves or sends instead, and plain <kbd>Enter</kbd> starts a new line.\n- <kbd>Esc</kbd> closes whatever is in front: a dialog, a card, an open panel. On the Metadata page,\n  with nothing in front and focus outside a text box, it takes you back to the article.\n\nThe article-navigation shortcuts leave keys alone while you are typing in a box. <kbd>⌘ Enter</kbd>\n/ <kbd>Ctrl Enter</kbd> is instead left to the box to save or send, and <kbd>Esc</kbd> can still\nclose what is in front."
